    "scientific_diagnosis_conclusion": "The apparent 49.92% mean prediction sensitivity is driven by a dual artifact: (1) An isolated heavy-tailed outlier (Instance 13, a K-12 School of 93,218 sq ft) where +5% GFA crosses a dense cluster of partition thresholds (diverging 91.3% of all 150 trees) and produces an isolated 1026.73% relative surge, single-handedly accounting for 41.07 percentage points (82.3%) of the overall mean. (2) Step-function extrapolation in piecewise-constant tree leaves amplified by the expm1() inverse transformation. Across the remaining 96% of the test cohort, the median response is a negligible 2.42%, confirming that the sensitivity is an isolated threshold-crossing artifact rather than a systemic model defect."
